      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The common target is to have one full year of your salary saved by the time you turn thirty.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "1× salary",
          "label": "the classic target by 30",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Saving is simply the income you set aside instead of spending.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-saving",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · saving"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The reality? The median under thirty-five has about thirty-nine thousand, so most people are behind.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$39K",
          "label": "median — most are behind",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "If that stings, here's the good news. The amount matters far less than the time.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "bank",
          "kicker": "don't panic",
          "line": "Time beats amount",
          "sub": "starting matters most"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Compound interest means early dollars grow the most.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
